! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1260's OP and AD blocks -- the deck's own
! tests that an invalid operation code sets OP and an invalid address
! sets AD.  PDF pp.41-42 (printed pp.38-39), octal
! 017225.00-017234.40, transcribed VERBATIM at the listing's own
! addresses and checked bit-exactly by
! verify_ax5b_16082_16083_listing.py.
!
! WHY THESE TWO.  They are contiguous, they are the only other blocks
! on pp.41-44 whose every instruction this project already implements
! (see docs/archival_inventory.md's triage of the sixteen), and
! together they print the SAME branch target through TWO different
! indicator numbers:
!
!     BOP,16088   21400.47 C2      indicator 15
!     BAD,16088   21400.50 42      indicator 16
!
! THAT PAIR IS THE POINT.  A branch-on-indicator half-word puts the
! 6-bit indicator number at bits 19-24, and the listing prints bits
! 18-23 as an octal pair and 24-31 as hex -- so the indicator number
! STRADDLES the boundary between the two printed fields, five bits in
! one and one bit in the other.  Two rows with the same address and
! adjacent indicator numbers therefore differ in BOTH printed fields
! at once, which is a sharper check of that field's placement than any
! single row can be.  15 and 16 differ in four of their six bits.
!
! AND THEY CORROBORATE A PAGE FROM A DIFFERENT ONE.  Both rows encode
! their target's bit 18 as ONE, so 16088 is at 021400.40.  That was
! established from pp.43-45 (see ax5b_16086_ds.strap); these two rows
! are on pp.41-42 and say it again, independently of that reading.
!
! NOTE, because the check cannot say it: L16088's 021400.40 is a SYN
! below, an INPUT to verify_ax5b_16082_16083_listing.py, chosen so the
! rows match.  The witness is the PRINTED code -- ".47" is 100111 and
! ".50" is 101000, both with bit 18 set -- read off pp.41-42 at 600
! dpi.  What the rows add is that this assembler places bit 18 where
! the listing places it.
!
! WHAT THE PAGE ITSELF SAYS.  Five comments on these fifteen rows:
! "-OP", "-UNABLE TO TURN OP ON.", "-AD", "-UNABLE TO TURN AD ON.",
! and nothing else.  Below, what is grounded and what is not.
!
! GROUNDED IN THE PAGE OR THE MANUAL:
!   LX,$X4,160K7 / SX,$X4,16082A
!                      LX and SX move a whole 64-bit word (Reference
!                      Manual p.23: LOAD INDEX replaces the index word
!                      "by the FULL-WORD specified by bits 0-17 of the
!                      effective address"; the section's opening
!                      paragraph names LX and SX as "the two
!                      exceptions [that] ... require full-word
!                      operands").  So the constant at 160K7 is copied
!                      over the whole of 16082A.
!   16082A XW,0,0,0    an all-zero full word, and the destination of
!                      that store.  Its printed code is
!                      "0.00 00 000000.00 00" -- both half-words zero.
!   BOP,16088 / BAD,16088
!                      branch on indicator 15 (OP, "operation code
!                      invalid", Ref. Manual p.23's programming note
!                      names it) and on indicator 16 (AD).  Taken
!                      means the indicator came on; falling through
!                      reaches SIC,SEN / B,SERS and the deck's
!                      "UNABLE TO TURN ... ON." message.
!   SV,$X4,1.32        the AD provocation.  Word 1 bits 28-63 are the
!                      time clock; the deck's own comment on the same
!                      instruction in 16086 (p.43) reads "TURN ON $AD
!                      ON".
!   CNOP               emits NOTHING here: the location counter is at
!                      017227.00 after the second NOP, already
!                      word-aligned, and the listing prints no address
!                      beside it.  16082A needs the alignment because
!                      XW is a full word.
!
! NOT TRACED, and left as a question rather than a guess:
!   * WHAT 160K7 CONTAINS.  Only its address, 023050.00, is printed
!     here.  The block's SHAPE -- store a word over a zeroed full-word
!     slot, two NOPs, then fall straight INTO that slot -- reads like
!     self-modifying code planting an invalid operation code to be
!     executed, which is what "-OP" and "UNABLE TO TURN OP ON." would
!     require.  Nothing on these pages says so, and 160K7 is not on
!     them.  Note also that a zero half-word decodes as BE,0 (BranchOr
!     Misc code 000), so what 16082A holds BEFORE the store is not
!     inert -- which is a reason the store must land, not evidence
!     about what it stores.
!
! WHAT THIS IS AND IS NOT.  An ENCODING oracle, like
! ax5b_16086_ds.strap and ibox1_ensu.strap.  It is NOT run on the
! model: both blocks fall through into the SEN/SERS error harness and
! 16093, none of which is transcribed, and 160K7's value is unknown.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS: one, the same systematic one as the 16086 block.
! This deck labels its blocks with NUMBERS (16082, 16082A, 16083,
! 16093, 16088) and this assembler reads a leading digit as an
! address, so every such label is prefixed with "L".  Nothing else is
! changed.

! External symbols, given by SYN at the addresses this same listing
! prints for them.  Rows naming one check the opcode and modifier bits
! only; their address came from the same print.  L16082A is defined
! INSIDE the range, so the row naming it is a real address check.
L160K7  SYN, (8)23050.0            ! the constant stored over 16082A
SEN     SYN, (8)1310.0             ! the SIC error-entry link
SERS    SYN, (8)1304.0             ! the error-report routine
L16093  SYN, (8)21734.0            ! the "next test" exit
L16088  SYN, (8)21400.40           ! the per-indicator interrupt walk;
                                   !   .40 -- see the header

        SLC, (8)17225.0
L16082  LX,  $X4, L160K7           ! -OP
        SX,  $X4, L16082A          !              over the zeroed slot
        NOP
        NOP
        CNOP                       !              emits nothing: already
                                   !              word-aligned
L16082A XW,  0, 0, 0               !              the slot, all zeros
        BOP, L16088                !              OP came on -> on we go
        SIC, SEN
        B,   SERS                  ! -UNABLE TO TURN OP ON.
        B,   L16093
L16083  SV,  $X4, 1.32             ! -AD          store into the time
                                   !              clock's word
        NOP
        BAD, L16088                !              AD came on -> on we go
        SIC, SEN
        B,   SERS                  ! -UNABLE TO TURN AD ON.
        B,   L16093
        END, L16082
